From c7fdac398e166644c6ac0629dbfdfabd3e96aab6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:06:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] test(app-audit): the borrowed probe takes scoped options;
 add its negative
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red: app-is-used (culprit 76f66a5d)
  the React audit borrows the probe instead of growing its own
    pinned `await probeControls(page, probeOpts())`

Decision: P. 76f66a5d gave the shared options a form scope and route:
probeOpts('desktop:/', '/') and probeOpts(`desktop:${r}`, r). The probe is
still the one imported from behaviour-audit, with the same shared budget,
eyes and seen-forms set. The positive now accepts any arguments to
probeOpts(...). Added the missing NEGATIVE half of «borrows»: app-audit
defines no probeControls/judgeBehaviour of its own.

Non-vacuity:
  probe-homegrown: import dropped, a local probeControls defined
    ✕ the React audit borrows the probe instead of growing its own
    ✕ NEGATIVE — and the audit defines no probe of its own
    Expected pattern: not /(?:function|const|let|var)\s+(?:probeControls|judgeBehaviour)\b/
    RESTORED: sha256 identical
  probe-no-shared-opts: desktop probes get an inline options object
    ✕ the React audit borrows the probe instead of growing its own
    Expected pattern: /await probeControls\(page, probeOpts\([^)]*\)\)/
    RESTORED: sha256 identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
---
 api/src/__tests__/app-is-used.test.ts | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/api/src/__tests__/app-is-used.test.ts b/api/src/__tests__/app-is-used.test.ts
index acddac42..8272e723 100644
--- a/api/src/__tests__/app-is-used.test.ts
+++ b/api/src/__tests__/app-is-used.test.ts
@@ -23,10 +23,21 @@ describe('one definition of a dead control', () => {
     it('the React audit borrows the probe instead of growing its own', () => {
         const A = read('core', 'quality', 'app-audit.ts');
         expect(A).toMatch(/import \{ probeControls, judgeBehaviour, FormResult, ControlResult \} from '\.\/behaviour-audit'/);
-        expect(A).toMatch(/await probeControls\(page, probeOpts\(\)\)/);
+        //  The shared options now carry the form's scope and route (76f66a5d),
+        //  so the call reads `probeOpts('desktop:/', '/')` — still the shared
+        //  budget, eyes and seen-forms set, still the borrowed probe.
+        expect(A).toMatch(/await probeControls\(page, probeOpts\([^)]*\)\)/);
         expect(A).toMatch(/judgeBehaviour\(allControls, behaviourMetrics/);
     });
 
+    it('NEGATIVE — and the audit defines no probe of its own', () => {
+        //  «Borrows» has two halves: the import above, and nothing local
+        //  standing in for it. A second definition is how two meanings of a
+        //  dead control come back.
+        const A = read('core', 'quality', 'app-audit.ts');
+        expect(A).not.toMatch(/(?:function|const|let|var)\s+(?:probeControls|judgeBehaviour)\b/);
+    });
+
     it('and the HTML builder still reaches it by the same road', () => {
         const B = read('core', 'quality', 'behaviour-audit.ts');
         expect(B).toMatch(/export async function probeControls/);
